secrets.error.identity_unreadable
  "private/identity.age is not a passphrase-encrypted age key. Restore it from the repo's history."

secrets.error.empty_recipients
  "private/recipients.txt has no public key in it. Restore it from the repo's history."

secrets.error.reserved
  "Refusing to write over /path/to/path: it is not a secret."

secrets.error.unsupported_ssh_key
  "Line 3 of private/recipients.txt holds a key age cannot encrypt to (<key_type>). Use an ssh-ed25519 key, or an ssh-rsa key of at least 2048 bits; homebot never seals to fewer keys than the file lists."

secrets.error.save_key
  "Saving the new key to /path/to/path failed; nothing was saved."

secrets.error.save_gitignore
  "Writing /path/to/path failed, so nothing was set up: without it, git would take the plaintext secrets in private/."

guard.check_failed
  "Could not check the staged files: <message>"

guard.not_home
  "/path/to/repo has no homebot.yml, so this commit can't be checked. Refusing."

guard.not_sealed
  "/path/to/file_path is named like a sealed file but is not age-encrypted. Unstage it:"
  "  git rm --cached /path/to/file_path"

guard.hooks_path_overridden
  "core.hooksPath is <path> after homebot set it to /path/to/want: a worktree config or an include overrides it, so the commit guard would not run. Remove that setting."

guard.private_gitlink
  "/path/to/file_path is a repository (a submodule or an embedded repo). Only *.age files may be committed from private/. Unstage it:"
  "  git rm --cached /path/to/file_path"

guard.private_not_folder
  "/path/to/file_path is staged as a symlink or a file, not a folder: committing it would drop every sealed secret from the repo. Make private a real folder again, then unstage it:"
  "  git rm --cached /path/to/file_path"

guard.all_sealed_deleted
  "This commit deletes all 3 sealed files in private/ and leaves none: private/ is missing, moved or emptied. If that is a mistake, put it back and unstage the deletions with the first command. If you mean to remove your secrets from the repo, commit with git yourself, in the home repo, with the second:"
  "  git restore --staged private"
  "  git commit --no-verify -- private"

guard.all_sealed_deleted (1)
  "This commit deletes 1 sealed file in private/ and leaves none: private/ is missing, moved or emptied. If that is a mistake, put it back and unstage the deletions with the first command. If you mean to remove your secrets from the repo, commit with git yourself, in the home repo, with the second:"
  "  git restore --staged private"
  "  git commit --no-verify -- private"

pack.error.private_reserved
  "/path/to/path can't go into private/: git would stage it as plaintext there. README.md, .gitignore, .gitkeep and recipients.txt files, *.age files and .git folders are the repo's own; rename or remove it first."

pack.error.nested_repo
  "/path/to/path is a git repository of its own: the home repo would hold only a pointer to it, and its files would never reach the remote. Remove its .git, or leave it out of the home."

pack.error.unreadable
  "Can't read /path/to/path, so homebot can't check it for a git repository of its own. Nothing was moved; make it readable, or leave it out of the home."

pack.error.layer_not_linked
  "The <layer> layer is not linked on <os>, so a file packed there could not be linked back (use <layers>)."

pack.error.source_not_removed
  "Copied /path/to/path into the repo as /path/to/repo_path, but could not remove the original: <reason>"
