help.persona.usage
  "homebot persona [command]"

help.persona.summary
  "list and manage personas"

help.persona.about
  "List, inspect, create, and choose the voice homebot speaks in."

help.persona.option.from
  "copy an existing persona's header and lines when creating a new one"

help.persona.option.event
  "preview one voiced message id"

help.persona.option.all_variants
  "show every valid variant in a preview"

help.persona.list.usage
  "homebot persona list"

help.persona.list.summary
  "list the personas you can choose"

help.persona.list.about
  "Lists the built-in personas and the files in your personas folder, one per line:"
  "a * on the one in use, its id, name, where it comes from and its tagline."
  "A persona that cannot be used shows why in place of its name."

help.persona.show.usage
  "homebot persona show <id>"

help.persona.show.summary
  "show a persona's header, colours and sample lines"

help.persona.show.about
  "Shows a persona's emoji, name and tagline, its three colours (accent, ok and"
  "muted, for light and dark terminals) and a few of its lines in its own voice."

help.persona.use.usage
  "homebot persona use <id|none>"

help.persona.use.summary
  "choose the persona for this home repo"

help.persona.use.about
  "Writes persona: in homebot.yml, after checking that the persona exists and"
  "loads. none turns the voice off. The shell's nudge and prompt symbol are"
  "refreshed at once."

help.persona.new.usage
  "homebot persona new <id>"

help.persona.new.summary
  "start a persona file of your own"

help.persona.new.about
  "Writes personas/<id>.toml in your config folder and never overwrites a file."
  "Without --from it extends neatpik and lists every voiced message as a comment;"
  "with --from it starts from a copy of that persona's header, language, colours"
  "and lines."

help.persona.validate.usage
  "homebot persona validate [id|file]"

help.persona.validate.summary
  "check a persona and the personas it extends"

help.persona.validate.about
  "Checks a persona and every persona it extends, and prints each problem with"
  "the file it is in. Give an id, or the path of a file you have not installed"
  "yet. Without one it checks the persona this home repo selects."

help.persona.preview.usage
  "homebot persona preview <id>"

help.persona.preview.summary
  "see a persona in light and dark terminals"

help.persona.preview.about
  "Shows the inbox, the shell nudge, the notification and the save results in"
  "the persona's voice, once for a light and once for a dark terminal. --event"
  "shows one voiced message id; --all-variants shows every valid variant."

help.persona.ids.usage
  "homebot persona ids"

help.persona.ids.summary
  "list the message ids a persona can give lines for"

help.persona.ids.about
  "Lists every voiced message id with its English text and its placeholders:"
  "the ids a persona file can give lines for."

